# PDF text is a layout serialisation, not a string

`pdftotext -layout` serialises the **visual** layout of a PDF. A value that overflows its
cell wraps, and the columns beside it are interleaved into the same lines. A semantically
continuous field is therefore **not** guaranteed to be a contiguous substring:

```
Nama Pasien     Miss Marcella O'Conner     No. Rekam Medis     MRN-U8XPPPBS
                DVM
```

This took down the one authorised consolidated Full Suite (run 32700184849) on a receipt
that was completely correct.

## Rules

1. **Never** assert a wrap-capable dynamic value is contiguous in PDF-extracted text:

   ```php
   expect($text)->toContain($visit->patient->name);   // FORBIDDEN
   ```

   Read the field out of its own column instead:

   ```php
   expect(pdfLayoutFieldValue($text, 'Nama'))->toBe($visit->patient->name);
   expect(pdfLayoutColumnText($text, 'Jenis Perawatan', 'Qty'))->toContain(pdfNormalizeText($item->description));
   expect(pdfLayoutFullWidthText($text))->toContain(pdfNormalizeText($branch->name));
   ```

   Helpers live in `tests/Pest.php` beside `pdfExtractText`. `FullSuiteBaselineContractTest`
   enforces this.

2. **Do not** flatten the page or strip all whitespace to make the match work. That fuses
   adjacent columns and matches values that were never printed. Per-token containment is
   equally unsafe — the tokens exist elsewhere.

3. **Do not fix a test flake in the runtime.** If the PDF contains all required semantic
   content and only extraction contiguity differs, the *test contract* is wrong. Changing
   valid escaping, CSS, column width or font to satisfy a brittle assertion hides the
   defect. Escalate instead if the document genuinely clips, overlaps or loses characters.

4. **Length, not escaping.** A long name with no apostrophe fails identically; a short name
   with one passes. Do not re-diagnose this as the faker-vs-Blade-escaping class — that
   reading is disproven and `e()` fixes nothing here.

5. **Pin the fixture.** A test covering wrapping must use a deterministic value known to
   wrap; faker entered the branch on ~6% of runs. Do not encode a character threshold — the
   wrap point is a proportional-font pixel width. Assert the *behaviour* (that the fixture
   still wraps) so the coverage claim fails loudly instead of silently lapsing.

6. Every new negative control must prove a **wrong** or **partially rendered** value still
   fails. A wrap-tolerant assertion that cannot fail is worse than the brittle one.

7. **Two-column pages interleave rows** (REVISION-RME-VISIT-DETAIL-INVOICE-REGISTRATION-UX-1).
   When a labelled block sits BESIDE another block, each of its lines can be followed by a
   line holding only the OTHER column's text, and a wrapped tail may sit after it.
   `pdfLayoutFieldValue()` therefore continues a value only with a segment that starts in
   the value's own column (±2), skips lines that belong only to another column, and still
   closes the cell on a blank line or when the label column fills. It can only ever return
   less than the old reader, never more.

8. **Columns are placed per page.** `pdftotext -layout` re-bases each page's text grid on
   that page's own leftmost text, so a table that continues onto a page without the block
   beside it moves left in the text. `pdfLayoutColumnText()` measures its band on every
   page from that page's own repeated heading and joins the pages. Never assume a band
   measured on page 1 applies to page 2.

